<Layout
  title="GPT-6.1 Sol — A.I. — Rycode"
  description="GPT-6.1 Sol is an upgrade to GPT-6 Sol, released 29 September 2026."
  variant="ai"
>
  <article class="ai-model">
    <p class="ai-model-kicker">Frontier models</p>
    <h1 class="ai-model-title">GPT-6.1 Sol</h1>
    <p class="ai-model-dek">GPT-6.1 Sol is an upgrade to <a href="/ai/models/openai/gpt-6-sol/">GPT-6 Sol</a>, released 29 September 2026. List price is $2 input, $0.10 cached input, and $10 output per million tokens. OpenAI says it is near <a href="/ai/models/openai/gpt-6-astra/">GPT-6 Astra</a> on coding, computer use, and professional work at one-fifth of Astra’s standard input and output list prices. The API id is <code>gpt-6.1-sol</code>. It is not yet in Chat.</p>
    <hr class="ai-model-rule" />
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Training</h2>
    <p>Knowledge cutoff on the model page is 30 April 2026. OpenAI has not published a parameter count for GPT-6.1 Sol on the announce, the model page, or the system-card addendum. The addendum says this model uses the same types of data and training as GPT-6 Astra.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Inference</h2>
    <p><code>reasoning.effort</code> supports <code>low</code>, <code>medium</code> (default), <code>high</code>, <code>xhigh</code>, and <code>max</code>. <code>none</code> and <code>minimal</code> are not supported. Reasoning tokens are supported. Use the Responses API for tool calling. Chat Completions is supported without tool calling. OpenAI says GPT-6.1 Sol Ultrafast is coming in the coming days, with up to 8× faster token generation than this model’s standard speed in Codex.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Context</h2>
    <p>The documented context window is 1,050,000 tokens. Max output is 128,000 tokens. Inputs are text and images. Output is text. Audio and video are not supported.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Methods</h2>
    <p>GPT-6.1 Sol is in ChatGPT Work and Codex, and on the API as <code>gpt-6.1-sol</code>. It is not yet in Chat. Tools named for this model on the Responses API include web search, file search, image generation, code interpreter, hosted shell, apply patch, skills, computer use, MCP, and tool search. Streaming, function calling, and structured outputs are supported. Fine-tuning is not.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Benchmarking</h2>
    <p>OpenAI says GPT-6.1 Sol is near GPT-6 Astra on coding, computer use, and professional work at one-fifth of Astra’s standard input and output list prices. On DeepSWE v1.1, OpenAI says it matches Astra at roughly one-fifth the cost and beats GPT-6 Sol’s best score by 6.4 percentage points at a lower reasoning effort.</p>
    <p>The cell below is OpenAI’s announce chart at High effort. It is a company chart.</p>
    <div class="ai-model-table-wrap">
      <table class="ai-model-table ai-model-table--prose">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Eval</th>
            <th scope="col">GPT-6.1 Sol</th>
            <th scope="col">Notes</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>DeepSWE v1.1</td><td>75.2%</td><td>Company announce chart, High effort (0.7522)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Access and pricing</h2>
    <p>Available to Plus, Pro, Business, Enterprise, and Edu users in ChatGPT Work and Codex, and to developers on the API as <code>gpt-6.1-sol</code>. Not yet in Chat.</p>
    <div class="ai-model-table-wrap">
      <table class="ai-model-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col"></th>
            <th scope="col">GPT-6.1 Sol</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Input / MTok</td><td>$2</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Cached input / MTok</td><td>$0.10</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Cache writes / MTok</td><td>$2.50</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Output / MTok</td><td>$10</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>Prompts with more than 272K input tokens are priced at 2× input and cache rates and 1.5× output for the full request.</p>
